The core of a game $v \in \mathcal{G}^{N,\mathcal{A}}$ is the set of preimputations for which the excess of any feasible coalition is non-positive:
\begin{equation*}
\text{core}(v) := \left\{ x\in \mathbb{R}^{N} \colon x (N) = v(N) \text{ and } e(S, x) \leq 0, \forall S \in \mathcal{A}^\ast \right\}.
\end{equation*}

A set of coalitions $\mathcal{S} \subseteq \mathcal{A}$ is a balanced set system if there exists a balancing weight system $\lambda_S \in \mathbb{R}_+$, $S \in \mathcal{S}$ such that

\begin{equation*}
\sum \limits_{S \in \mathcal{S}} \lambda_S \, \chi_S = \chi_N,
\end{equation*}

\noindent where $\chi_T \in \mathbb{R}^N$ is the characteristic vector of set $T$.

